load @/code/group
  find group

# A group homomorphism: a map between two groups that respects their operations, so the image of a product is the
# product of the images. It is the structure-preserving map of group theory, the arrow that lets two groups be compared.
# Its kernel (what maps to the identity) and its image are themselves groups, and the first isomorphism theorem relates
# them. The form carries the source and target groups; the operation-preserving law is the defining condition.
form group-homomorphism
  link source, like group
  link target, like group
